CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --unwind 4 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ first_type<A\.\.\.>::type resolves to long long \(8 bytes\): SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[temp.variadic] + [expr.sizeof]/5: a deduced function-template parameter pack A
used as a class-template argument (first_type<A...>) names the correct member
via the dependent qualified-id first_type<A...>::type.  The qualified-id
resolution already expanded the pack; the failure was that
sizeof(first_type<A...>::type) was mis-evaluated as a sizeof...(pack) pack-size
query (returning the pack count) because the parser did not distinguish
`sizeof...` from `sizeof`.  Fixed by marking `sizeof...` in the parser and only
counting pack elements for that genuine form.

A decltype-valued variant of the trait is exercised by
cpp11_decltype_pack_in_class_template.  Part of the unified pack-expansion
rework documented in doc/architectural/cpp-variadic-pack-expansion-rework.md.
